## Interface: 30300
## Title: |cff1784d1DragonUI|r |cffffffffNew Era|r
## Notes: Dragonflight-style panels for 3.3.5a — downport of NewEra (Classic 1.15) onto DragonUI.
## Author: DragonUI_NewEra team
## Version: 0.1.0
## Dependencies: DragonUI, !!!ClassicAPI
## OptionalDeps: DragonUI_Options
## SavedVariables: DragonUI_NewEraDB

bootstrap.lua

# --- libs: embedded so features don't depend on other addons being loaded ---
# LibCustomGlow provides the WeakAuras-style "Action Button Glow" (ants) used for the spellbook's
# active-ability indicator. Embedded (not relying on WeakAuras); LibStub dedupes if another copy loads.
Libs\LibStub\LibStub.lua
Libs\LibCustomGlow-1.0\LibCustomGlow-1.0.xml

# --- compat: thin bridge over the REQUIRED !!!ClassicAPI (owner: API Bridge Engineer) ---
# !!!ClassicAPI is a hard dependency and loads first (via its !!! prefix + Dependencies), so it
# owns the modern globals (C_Timer/C_Texture/C_Container/C_Item/C_Spell/C_SpellBook/C_Map/Mixin/…).
# These files now only fill the handful of symbols ClassicAPI does NOT provide; C_Timer/C_Texture
# are fully ClassicAPI-owned and no longer shipped here. See compat/COVERAGE.md.
compat\Compat.lua
# Events.lua adds Frame:RegisterUnitEvent (a 5.0 API; ClassicAPI implements the semantics but only
# inside its private namespace) plus NE.EV_LEARNED_SPELL. Must follow Compat.lua for NE.compat.
compat\Events.lua
compat\C_Container.lua
compat\C_Item.lua
compat\C_Spell.lua
compat\C_Map.lua
compat\SpellBook.lua

compat\Locale.lua
Locales\Load_Locales.xml

# --- core: downported NewEra Core chrome toolkit (owner: Core/Chrome Engineer) ---
core\FrameUtil.lua
core\Scale.lua
# PanelManager = the one coordinator for the standalone panel windows (they all hard-code a default
# anchor and several picked the same one — issue #49). Loads before every module, since each window
# builder calls NE.panelmgr.Register at the end of its build.
core\PanelManager.lua
core\Texture.lua
core\NineSlice.lua
core\NineSliceLayouts.lua
core\PanelChrome.lua
core\Portrait.lua
core\Tabs.lua
# Menu = a MenuUtil-shaped context-menu builder over UIDropDownMenu. Resolves its backend lazily,
# so it does not care where ClassicAPI sits in the load order.
core\Menu.lua
# NavBar = retail's breadcrumb bar, ONCE. It was rebuilt from scratch more than once on this
# client, and the later copy re-introduced two faults the first had already fixed (Home sitting on
# the window portrait; crumbs drawn under their own bar's regions). This is the Adventure Guide's
# implementation, which was the better of them, with the trail handed in by the caller.
# Needs NE.tex + NE.nineslice, both above.
core\NavBar.lua
core\ButtonSkin.lua
# Squelch = keep a Blizzard region hidden for good (a Show-swap for textures, an OnShow
# re-hide for frames). Every reskin here has needed it: the cases that forced it into core are
# the ones where the client re-Shows its own chrome from a path we do not own, and there is no
# single update hook to sweep from.
core\Squelch.lua
# MaxMin = the retail maximize/minimize button. 3.3.5a ships no MaximizeMinimizeButtonFrame
# template, so it is BUILT rather than reskinned. Art is the RedButton family on sheet
# 4698972, registered in NineSliceLayouts above — so this must load after it.
core\MaxMin.lua
core\ScrollbarReskin.lua
core\ItemButton.lua
core\ItemGrid.lua
core\Modules.lua
# --- core: HUD-layer primitives (added for the Cooldown Manager port; reusable) ---
# GridLayout    = Lua reimplementation of retail's GridLayoutFrame template (absent on 3.3.5a).
# CooldownNumbers = countdown text on Cooldown frames (the widget draws none on this client).
# AuraSnapshot  = one UnitBuff/UnitDebuff walk per unit per frame, shared addon-wide.
# SpellRanks    = per-ability rank ids from the live spellbook. Load-bearing: GetSpellInfo's 7th
#                 return is castTime here, NOT the spellID it is on modern clients.
core\GridLayout.lua
core\CooldownNumbers.lua
core\AuraSnapshot.lua
core\SpellRanks.lua

# --- textures: art + atlas registration data (owner: Asset Pipeline Engineer) ---
Textures\Assets.lua

