# --- Inspect (modern chrome on the LoadOnDemand Blizzard_InspectUI window) ---
# A RESKIN, not a replacement: on 3.3.5a InspectFrame is a bare 384x512 frame whose three tab
# subframes (PaperDoll / PVP / Talent) own all of the wooden art and all of the content, and the
# PvP and Talents panes are Blizzard's to keep -- scaled and anchored so their content lands on the
# one window size every tab uses. Load order: InspectFrame (chrome, tabs, geometry + the pane fit)
# -> PaperDoll (the Character tab re-laid-out to DragonUI's character-panel geometry) ->
# Register (the reload-gated module entry + the ADDON_LOADED gate the LoD window needs).
# See modules/inspect/PORT_NOTES.md for what the 1.15 source has that this client cannot.
modules\inspect\InspectFrame.lua
modules\inspect\PaperDoll.lua
# The PVP tab, drawn on our own furniture over the client's inspect-honor/arena data. The native
# InspectPVPFrame stays loaded and keeps driving that data; only its content is squelched.
modules\inspect\PvPPane.lua
modules\inspect\Register.lua

# --- Merchant (modern chrome on the client's vendor window; downport of NewEra/MerchantFrame) ---
# A RESKIN, not a replacement: FrameXML keeps MerchantFrame_Update and all of the buy/sell/repair
# behaviour, and we re-dress the frame it paints on. Load order: Assets (sheets + atlas rects; must
# precede every SetAtlas call) -> MerchantFrame (chrome, rows, per-update sync, and the deferred
# build) -> the two added buttons, whose builders MerchantFrame's build pass calls -> Register (the
# reload-gated module entry). See modules/merchant/PORT_NOTES.md for what the 1.15 source has that
# this client cannot.
modules\merchant\Assets.lua
modules\merchant\MerchantFrame.lua
modules\merchant\SellAllJunk.lua
modules\merchant\BuybackUndo.lua
# /nemerchant — report-only state dump. A desaturated icon and an icon that never resolved look the
# same on screen; this prints which one it is.
modules\merchant\Diagnostics.lua
modules\merchant\Register.lua

